    \"\"\"Lazily build the shared async Redis client. Short timeouts so a slow/down\n     Redis fails fast into the fail-open path rather than stalling the request.\n     \"\"\"\ndiff --git a/backend/requirements-typecheck.txt b/backend/requirements-typecheck.txt\nindex 94f251af8..a27ecd897 100644\n--- a/backend/requirements-typecheck.txt\n+++ b/backend/requirements-typecheck.txt\n@@ -24,9 +24,10 @@ httpx==0.28.1\n psycopg2-binary==2.9.13\n pydantic==2.13.5\n pydantic-settings==2.16.1\n+# redis-py ships its own types (py.typed); the old types-redis stubs described 4.x.\n+redis==7.4.1\n sqlalchemy[mypy]==2.0.57\n structlog==26.1.0\n types-jsonschema==4.26.0.20261006\n-types-redis==4.6.0.20241004\n types-openpyxl==3.1.5.20260827\n types-PyYAML==6.0.12.20260906\ndiff --git a/backend/requirements.txt b/backend/requirements.txt\nindex ac0d57576..b5dae515c 100644\n--- a/backend/requirements.txt\n+++ b/backend/requirements.txt\n@@ -21,8 +21,8 @@ anthropic==1.15.0                  # MIT (rule 40); the LLMProvider seam's Anthr\n httpx==0.28.1                     # the backend's outbound HTTP client — Teams/Slack alerting, ADF + Airflow polling, Marquez lineage, the OpenBao secret store (ADR 0039). Was dev-only and reached prod transitively via openlineage, i.e. unpinned from our side (#1055)\n \n # ── Task queue ──\n-celery[redis]==5.6.3\n-redis==5.3.1\n+celery[redis]==5.7.0\n+redis==7.4.1\n croniter==6.2.4                   # cron-expression parsing for suite run schedules (A7)\n \n # ── Database ──\ndiff --git a/changelog.d/2743.changed.md b/changelog.d/2743.changed.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..f2802c139\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/changelog.d/2743.changed.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\n+**The task queue runs on Celery 5.7 and redis-py 7.4.** Celery 5.7 needs a newer Redis client\n+than the 5.x line DataQ pinned, so the two move together. Nothing changes for the API, the\n+worker or the scheduler: every Redis client still fails fast on its own short timeouts.","is_error":fal